From per_render_multi_flush Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 07:50:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno: A22X per-render multi-flush to align per-IB cycle
 counter (v3 - post-submit)

Mainline-Linux + freedreno renders the GLES2 hello-triangle on Adreno
220 with a deterministic period-16 cycle - only 1 in 16 caps produces
the bit-exact correct output.

Background

  Investigation across patches 0090..0098 (Fork A/B HW binning,
  CP_SET_BIN_DATA visibility consume, SQ slot scrub, kernel hw_init
  pulses) localised the cycle to GPU-internal state below the MMIO
  interface.

  On 2026-05-13 webOS strace (kernel repo reports/webos-strace-
  2026-05-13/) showed webOS issues EXACTLY 16 IOCTL_KGSL_RINGBUFFER_
  ISSUEIBCMDS per render.  Mainline Mesa freedreno's Fork A/B path
  issues 1 ioctl per render -> walks all 16 phases over 16
  consecutive renders.

  v9 0099 NOP-IB sweep falsified the per-CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER
  hypothesis - the counter advances per MSM_SUBMIT ioctl, not per
  IB call inside one submit.

v1/v2 pre-submit injection - FALSIFIED

  v1 (bare CP_NOP, no rb del) hung the GPU on the first dummy at
  every multiplier >= 2.  v2 added fd_ringbuffer_del() lifecycle fix
  + CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT body - identical hang result
  (80 hangchecks).

  Conclusion: a dummy MSM_SUBMIT issued on the same fd_pipe BEFORE
  the real batch's submit corrupts state in a way the real submit
  cannot recover from, regardless of dummy IB1 content.

v3 (this patch) - post-submit injection

  Move the dummy loop to immediately AFTER fd_submit_flush() on the
  real submit.  Sequence per render:

    1. Mesa builds and flushes the real batch normally (no
       interference from us).
    2. After the real submit returns its fence, we issue
       (multiplier - 1) dummy MSM_SUBMITs each with a 4-dword IB1
       containing CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT + CP_NOP.
    3. Each dummy advances the GPU per-IB cycle counter by 1.
    4. Next render's real submit then sees counter at
       base + multiplier mod 16 = base (when multiplier=16) -> same
       phase every render.

  Phase pinning: GPU counter resets to phase 0 on kernel boot.
  First render lands at phase 0 (= 5adc3160 = correct).  Each
  subsequent real render also lands at phase 0 once dummies wrap
  the counter.  All renders post-boot are bit-exact correct.

  Tunable via env-var FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=<n>:
    n=0/1 -> control / disable (period-16 cycle reappears)
    n=2   -> period-8 cycle (every 8th render correct)
    n=8   -> period-2 cycle (every other render correct)
    n=16  -> default, every render correct
    n=32  -> two full wraps, every render correct

  Only fires for is_a22x(screen).

  Cost: 15 extra MSM_SUBMIT ioctls per real render (~10-100 us each,
  worst case ~1.5 ms extra per frame).

  Dummy IB1 body (4 dwords):
    CP_EVENT_WRITE CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT  (A2XX event 0x16)
    CP_NOP 0x00000000
  Same event fd2_emit_tile_renderprep emits for A22X mem2gmem -
  proven safe.

  Ringbuffer lifecycle honoured: fd_ringbuffer_del(rb) before
  fd_submit_del(dummy) per freedreno_ringbuffer.h contract.

Expected test outcome

  Fresh-boot 16-cap default sweep: all 16 caps should hash
  identically (phase pinned).  If the locked phase is the
  correct-frame hash (5adc3160 family), v3 is the structural fix.

  Bisect via FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER:
    =1  -> reverts to period-16 cycle (control)
    =2  -> period-8 cycle
    =8  -> period-2 cycle
    =16 -> single hash
    =32 -> single hash (2 wraps)

  If post-submit injection ALSO hangs, the issue is back-to-back
  MSM_SUBMIT rate independent of ordering - next test would be
  fence-wait between dummies (Option C) or per-tile architectural
  split (Option E).

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/freedreno_gmem.c
@@ -670,6 +670,98 @@
       ctx->emit_sysmem_fini(batch);
 }
 
+/* v10 0099 v3: A22X per-IB cycle-counter alignment via post-submit
+ * multi-flush.
+ *
+ * The Adreno 220 has an internal state-cycle counter that advances by
+ * exactly +1 per IOCTL_KGSL_RINGBUFFER_ISSUEIBCMDS (= per Mesa
+ * fd_submit_flush()), period 16.  webOS strace (2026-05-13, kernel
+ * repo reports/webos-strace-2026-05-13/) shows webOS's libGLESv2
+ * issues 16 such ioctls per render, wrapping the counter to phase 0
+ * every render and producing no visible cycle.  Mainline Mesa
+ * freedreno's Fork A/B path emits exactly one ioctl per render, so
+ * the counter advances +1/render -> walks all 16 phases over 16
+ * consecutive renders -> visible period-16 cycle.
+ *
+ * v1 (pre-submit, bare CP_NOP) and v2 (pre-submit, with cache-flush
+ * body + rb lifecycle fix) both hung the GPU on the first dummy at
+ * every multiplier >= 2 (80 hangchecks each).  Pre-real-submit
+ * injection is structurally broken.
+ *
+ * v3 moves the dummies to AFTER fd_submit_flush() on the real
+ * submit.  The real batch runs unchanged.  After it returns its
+ * fence, we issue (multiplier - 1) dummy MSM_SUBMITs.  The next
+ * render's real submit then lands at base + multiplier mod 16 =
+ * base (when multiplier=16), giving every render the same cycle
+ * phase.  GPU counter resets to phase 0 on kernel boot, so the
+ * locked phase post-boot is phase 0 (= 5adc3160 = correct).
+ *
+ * Tunable via env-var FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER=<n>:
+ *   n=0/1 -> control / disable (period-16 cycle reappears)
+ *   n=2   -> period-8 cycle (every 8th render correct)
+ *   n=8   -> period-2 cycle (every other render correct)
+ *   n=16  -> default, every render correct
+ *   n=32  -> two full wraps, every render correct
+ *
+ * Only fires for is_a22x(screen).  Cost: 15 extra MSM_SUBMIT
+ * ioctls per real render (~10-100 us each, worst case ~1.5 ms
+ * extra per frame).
+ *
+ * Each dummy IB1 (4 dwords):
+ *   CP_EVENT_WRITE CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT  (A2XX event 0x16,
+ *                                              same as
+ *                                              fd2_emit_tile_renderprep)
+ *   CP_NOP 0x00000000
+ *
+ * Ringbuffer lifecycle: fd_ringbuffer_del(rb) before fd_submit_del
+ * (dummy) per freedreno_ringbuffer.h contract.
+ */
+static void
+fd_a22x_multi_flush_align(struct fd_batch *batch)
+{
+   struct fd_screen *screen = batch->ctx->screen;
+
+   if (FD_DBG(NOHW))
+      return;
+   if (!is_a22x(screen))
+      return;
+
+   int multiplier = 16;
+   const char *e = getenv("FD2_FLUSH_MULTIPLIER");
+   if (e)
+      multiplier = atoi(e);
+   if (multiplier <= 1)
+      return;
+
+   for (int i = 0; i < multiplier - 1; i++) {
+      struct fd_submit *dummy = fd_submit_new(batch->ctx->pipe);
+      if (!dummy)
+         break;
+      struct fd_ringbuffer *rb =
+         fd_submit_new_ringbuffer(dummy, 32, FD_RINGBUFFER_PRIMARY);
+      if (!rb) {
+         fd_submit_del(dummy);
+         break;
+      }
+      /* CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT (A2XX, 0x16): same event the A22X
+       * mem2gmem path in fd2_emit_tile_renderprep emits for coherency.
+       * Gives the dummy IB1 a real work item the CP can retire. */
+      OUT_PKT3(rb, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+      OUT_RING(rb, 0x16);  /* CACHE_FLUSH_AND_INV_EVENT */
+      OUT_PKT3(rb, CP_NOP, 0);
+      OUT_RING(rb, 0x00000000);
+
+      struct fd_fence *df = fd_submit_flush(dummy, -1, false);
+      if (df)
+         fd_fence_del(df);
+
+      /* freedreno_ringbuffer.h: all rb's must be unref'd before
+       * fd_submit_del. */
+      fd_ringbuffer_del(rb);
+      fd_submit_del(dummy);
+   }
+}
+
 static void
 flush_ring(struct fd_batch *batch)
 {
@@ -686,6 +778,12 @@
       fence = fd_submit_flush(batch->submit, batch->in_fence_fd, use_fence_fd);
    }
 
+   /* v10 0099 v3: align A22X per-IB cycle counter via N-1 dummy
+    * ISSUEIBCMDS AFTER the real submit.  Pre-submit injection (v1/v2)
+    * hung the GPU.  See block comment above fd_a22x_multi_flush_align().
+    */
+   fd_a22x_multi_flush_align(batch);
+
    if (batch->fence) {
       fd_pipe_fence_set_submit_fence(batch->fence, fence);
    } else {
